## Why This Is Asked

Tests practical ability to apply basic AWS guardrails in a real-world multi-team setup.

## Key Concepts

- IAM least privilege with per-prefix access
- S3 bucket policy enforcement for encryption and public access
- Event-driven validation with Lambda on PutObject
- Observability via CloudWatch

## Code Example

```javascript
// Minimal Lambda skeleton to validate encryption and prefix
exports.handler = async (event) => {
  const r = event.Records[0];
  const bucket = r.s3.bucket.name;
  const key = r.s3.object.key;
  const enc = r.s3.object.serverSideEncryption;
  if (!enc) throw new Error("Object not encrypted");
  if (!/^corp-logs\/team-(a|b|c)\//.test(key)) throw new Error("Wrong prefix");
  return;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you scale this pattern for more teams?
- How would you test revocation and auditing of access?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests proficiency designing fine-grained, scalable access controls for multi-tenant data lakes using ABAC, tags, and policy syntax.

## Key Concepts
- IAM tags and aws:PrincipalTag
- Resource policies with aws:RequestTag and stringEquals conditions
- S3 bucket prefixes per tenant and least privilege
- Testing cross-tenant access and tag revocation

## Code Example
```json
// Trust policy (IAM role)
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Principal": {"AWS": "arn:aws:iam::ACCOUNT:role/TenantAccess"},
      "Action": "sts:AssumeRole",
      "Condition": {"StringEquals": {"aws:PrincipalTag/tenant-id": "${aws:PrincipalTag/tenant-id}"}}
    }
  ]
}
```
```json
// Permission policy
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": ["s3:GetObject"],
      "Resource": "arn:aws:s3:::data-lake/${aws:PrincipalTag/tenant-id}/*",
      "Condition": {"StringEquals": {"aws:RequestTag/tenant-id": "${aws:PrincipalTag/tenant-id}"}}
    }
  ]
}
```
```json
// Bucket policy (alternative strict guard)
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Principal": {"AWS": "arn:aws:iam::ACCOUNT:role/TenantAccess"},
      "Action": "s3:GetObject",
      "Resource": "arn:aws:s3:::data-lake/${aws:PrincipalTag/tenant-id}/*",
      "Condition": {"StringEquals": {"s3:ExistingObjectTag/tenant-id": "${aws:PrincipalTag/tenant-id}"}}
    }
  ]
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you rotate tags and ensure no stale access remains?
- How would you integrate with CI to validate policies in a sandbox before prod?
